  "brief": "IonQ to acquire Elisity in an all-stock deal valued at up to $1.3 billion, expanding its quantum security platform.\n\nIonQ / Elisity (Announced): IonQ to Acquire Elisity. IonQ is acquiring Elisity in a deal worth up to $1.3 billion [1, 2, 3]. The deal is valued at up to $1.3 billion and is expected to expand IonQ's quantum security platform [4, 5, 6]. The acquisition is an all-stock deal and has been announced by IonQ [7, 8].\nAmazon / Decart (Rumored): Amazon to Acquire AI Startup Decart. Amazon is reportedly in talks to acquire AI startup Decart for around $7 billion [10, 11, 12]. The deal is said to be in advanced talks, with Amazon nearing a $7 billion acquisition of the Israeli AI startup Decart [13, 14]. The talks echo a deal that changed Amazon's cloud business, with the $7 billion Decart acquisition potentially impacting Amazon's AI chip race [15]. Amazon's interest in Decart is seen as part of its efforts to strengthen its AI capabilities, with the acquisition potentially worth $7 billion [16, 17].\nAlbertsons / Kroger (Pending approval): Albertsons and Kroger Deal. Albertsons and Kroger are in a dispute over a failed merger [19, 20]. Albertsons is seeking more than $9 billion from Kroger [19, 20]. Albertsons claims Kroger was 'reckless' in handling a key consultant [21, 22].\nSTERIS / Xodus Medical (Announced): STERIS to Acquire Xodus Medical. STERIS is acquiring Xodus Medical [24]. The deal was announced on October 12 [23]. The acquisition will add operating-room supplies [23].\nSkyAI / Forward Industries (Announced): SkyAI and Forward Industries Deal. SkyAI plans a $3 per share cash tender offer for up to 95% of shares [26, 27]. SkyAI rejects Forward Industries bid [26, 27]. SkyAI plans a $3 per share cash tender offer [25].\nAscend Sport / Evonext (Announced): Ascend Sport and Evonext Deal. Ascend Sport and Evonext are merging to list on the Swiss Stock Exchange [28, 29, 30]. The deal was announced and no further updates are available [28, 29, 30].\nCredit Agricole / IKB (Announced): Credit Agricole Buys IKB from Lone Star Funds. Credit Agricole has agreed to buy IKB from Lone Star Funds [31]. The deal was announced on October 12, 2003 [31]. No further information is available [31].\nWeston family / Boots (Announced): Weston family to buy Boots. The Weston family is acquiring Boots in an $8.9 billion deal [33, 34, 35]. The deal was announced on October 7 [36, 37]. No further information is available [32].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Struggling Leicester City owners seek takeover bids this week [38].\n- Getty Images to File for Bankruptcy, Go Private In Restructuring Deal [39].\n- Iz Yatirim Holding Boosts Digital Portfolio with 25% Stake in Hızlı Çiçek [40].",
